1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:02,794
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:15,056
[emcee] <i>The beloved father</i>
<i>of our town has arrived! Governor Julio!</i>

3
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:19,519
<i>A very happy and prosperous</i>
<i>festival to all of us!</i>

4
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:20,812
[crowd cheering]

5
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,773
[Dante] <i>Yes, this is going to be</i>
<i>our new home!</i>

6
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:27,652
<i>The front yard is huge!</i>
<i>But why don't we have neighbors?</i>

7
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:30,572
[Camia] <i>No one will think</i>
<i>of doing us harm here.</i>

8
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:34,117
[Julio] <i>You're the one at fault</i>
<i>for all of this.</i>

9
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,494
<i>If a married couple is having problems,</i>

10
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:38,747
<i>it's always the wife's fault.</i>

11
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,792
<i>You… You and your weaknesses as a woman…</i>

12
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:46,421
[Camia] <i>The Ardientes must be</i>
<i>very important people.</i>

13
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:49,799
[teacher] <i>The Ardientes provide</i>
<i>for this town's needs.</i>

14
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:52,802
<i>We're all so grateful to their family.</i>

15
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:57,348
<i>We pay for everything the politicians</i>
<i>do for us with our taxes.</i>

16
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,185
<i>We don't owe them anything.</i>
<i>It's not their money.</i>

17
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:03,980
[Julio] <i>Each given year,</i>
<i>you fail one subject in school!</i>

18
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:04,981
[Diego] <i>Grandpa!</i>

19
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,608
<i>I have to be brave.</i>

20
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>Hey, don't jump! Oh no!</i>
<i>Grab my hand! Hurry!</i>

21
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,863
[Lily] <i>You're hurt.</i>
<i>Do you want to come over?</i>

22
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>No, thanks. My family</i>
<i>might be looking for me.</i>

23
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:15,366
[Lily] <i>Take care, Diego.</i>

24
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,910
[Atty. Sta. Maria]
<i>Legal battles are rare here.</i>

25
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:19,454
<i>For the past 15 years,</i>
<i>there's practically been no crime!</i>

26
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:21,831
[Arthur] <i>That's not true!</i>
<i>This place is pure evil!</i>

27
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:23,625
<i>There'll come a day</i>
<i>this town will cease to exist.</i>

28
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,960
[Camia] <i>You come all the way</i>
<i>here to study?</i>

29
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,212
[Diego]<i> Yes. It's quiet here.</i>

30
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:30,423
<i>-We can help you if you want.</i>
-[Lily] <i>My mom's a teacher.</i>

31
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>You'll get better grades</i>
<i>if you let her help you.</i>

32
00:01:38,306 --> 00:01:39,891
-[Diego panting]
-[Lily] I'm tired!

33
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:42,477
[Lily] It's really beautiful here.

34
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,939
[shouting] I want to eat ice cream!

35
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:48,358
[exhales] Really?

36
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,485
-Yeah.
-Okay, I'll treat you to ice cream.

37
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:55,532
But you have to do
our exercises ten times first!

38
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,534
[Lily laughing]
So, do you still want ice cream?

39
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:01,538
[shouting] I don't want ice cream anymore!

40
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:04,207
[Lily laughing]
You changed your mind, huh?

41
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:08,086
Why do you always have that with you?

42
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,672
<i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>.

43
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:13,883
I love it when my father reads this to me.

44
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:18,471
I like reading about people's lives
changing for the better.

45
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:19,889
No matter how poor you might be,

46
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:22,642
you could be rich one day. [chuckles]

47
00:02:22,725 --> 00:02:25,603
Well…

48
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:30,358
being poor's fine
as long as I have a happy family.

49
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,902
Just like yours! That'd be great.

50
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,488
You can, though.
Just keep coming back to see us.

51
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:41,619
-Can I?
-Yes! Of course! Any time!

52
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:44,539
[shouting] Thank you, Lily!

53
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:48,877
Am I there?

54
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,296
-No.
-Am I deaf?

55
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:55,133
-No!
-Then you didn't have to shout!

56
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:57,135
[shouts] You're welcome, Diego!

57
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:58,928
-Like that?
-[both laughing]

58
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,972
-Let's go!
-Let's go there!

59
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,935
[Diego] What? I don't get it.

60
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,937
[Lily] Diego needs help, Mom.

61
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:11,107
I was trying to teach him,
but he still can't solve this.

62
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,942
[Camia] It's easy. Here…

63
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:16,487
[pensive music playing]

64
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:22,827
-[tense music playing]
-[inaudible]

65
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,789
-[Dante] Snack time!
-[Lily] Dad!

66
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:30,209
-Want some sandwiches?
-[Camia] Wow! Did you make these?

67
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:32,086
-[Dante] Of course!
-[Loring] Hey, Diego.

68
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,922
The driver's here to pick us up.

69
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,965
[Diego] Okay. Thank you.

70
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:38,968
-Bye!
-[Lily] Take care!

71
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:40,345
[Diego] Thank you!

72
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,721
-Come back, okay?
-[Diego] I'll be back!

73
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:50,939
[teacher 1] <i>Let's all rise</i>
<i>and welcome the Ardiente Family!</i>

74
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:52,065
<i>A round of applause for them!</i>

75
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:55,735
-[band playing lively tune]
-[people cheering and clapping]

76
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,660
Hi, Diego!

77
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:06,412
Hi, Lily.

78
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,473
Hi. I'm Raul Torillo.

79
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:27,850
I'm the husband of our lovely mayor.

80
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:31,104
Good afternoon, sir.
I'm Camia Cruz. I tutor Diego.

81
00:04:32,855 --> 00:04:33,898
Thank you.

82
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:37,568
[tense music playing]

83
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:43,199
See you.

84
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:46,703
[crowd cheering]

85
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:55,837
[Julio] Education is a valuable thing.
Especially to the youth.

86
00:04:56,587 --> 00:05:01,676
And last year, I noticed the lack of…

87
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:04,929
-Ms. Maan, I need to go to the restroom.
-…facilities…

88
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:07,265
-Sure.
-…in this school.

89
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,683
Just imagine

90
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:14,439
40 to 50 students
gathering in one classroom.

91
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:19,527
They must have felt
like sardines tightly packed

92
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,738
in one small can.

93
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,031
Where's the restroom?

94
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,532
-That way, sir.
-So, here, today…

95
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:26,409
I'll go to the restroom. Excuse me.

96
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:30,747
…I'm pleased to present
the newest building in this school!

97
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:34,000
[crowd clapping and cheering]

98
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:41,424
[foreboding music playing]

99
00:05:47,555 --> 00:05:49,599
[suspenseful music playing]

100
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:54,771
[whistles]

101
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:58,441
Sir.

102
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:02,612
Sorry, I thought this was the men's room.

103
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:05,239
-The men's room's over there.
-Oh, is that so?

104
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:13,873
So, you're the one
tutoring my son for free.

105
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,793
You're so kind. Thank you.

106
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,962
-It's nothing. Excuse me.
-Wait.

107
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,883
Why are you in a hurry?

108
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,468
I still want to talk to you.

109
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,303
Sir, we can talk outside.

110
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:29,889
What's wrong with talking here?

111
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:35,103
Now I know why my son
is so inspired to study.

112
00:06:37,313 --> 00:06:38,981
You're more beautiful up close.

113
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,483
Sir, please take your hands off me.

114
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:41,818
I'm just saying you're beautiful.

115
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:46,239
I said take your hands off me!
Don't touch me!

116
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:52,370
Sir! Let me go! Let me go!

117
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:53,955
-[pot breaking]
-[heavy breathing]

118
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:03,339
[Julio] <i>Good day to everyone!</i>

119
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:07,176
<i>I hope you can make good use</i>
<i>of the new building.</i>

120
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,803
[crowd clapping]

121
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:16,394
-Be careful, kids!
-Ms. Maan, where's Lily?

122
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:18,771
She's over there.

123
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:22,650
What happened to you?

124
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:27,530
Why are you shaking? Are you all right?

125
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,209
[music stops]

126
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,378
[Dante] What happened to you?

127
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,297
Lily said she saw you
trembling at school today.

128
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:49,302
What? It's nothing, hon.
I was just stressed.

129
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:53,764
There were a lot of people. How was work?

130
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:56,184
It was all right.

131
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:59,520
You know, I was thinking.

132
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,023
All the records I found
at the office say that this town

133
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,774
has an almost zero crime rate.

134
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:07,695
But there were a lot of accidents.

135
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:11,657
For example, car accidents
where people die.

136
00:08:11,741 --> 00:08:14,577
Hon, where is this leading to?

137
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:18,164
All the crimes, ambush, murder,

138
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:22,293
all happened a few kilometers away
from the town boundaries.

139
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:26,339
All the people
who got involved with the Ardientes

140
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,883
were all found dead outside town.

141
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:31,719
-It might be a coincidence.
-And another thing.

142
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:36,140
There are graft charges
against Emilia and the Governor.

143
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,475
As for Raul Torillo,

144
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,311
he's got rape charges against him.

145
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:41,604
Stop this.

146
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:45,358
But hon, if it's true,
the victims need justice!

147
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:54,158
[tense music playing]

148
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:12,802
[tense music playing]

149
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:21,269
What are you doing? [moans]

150
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:23,729
You're so beautiful, Camia.

151
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,235
What did you say? Who's Camia?

152
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,655
What? I didn't say that.

153
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:35,866
-I heard you say "Camia".
-Shh. I didn't say anything.

154
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:39,036
-You said Camia. Who is she?
-Who's "Camia"?

155
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,415
I said, "Come here, Emilia."

156
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:45,001
You're such a liar.

157
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,545
You know what? You have a lot of issues.

158
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:48,879
I'm leaving.

159
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:55,428
ARDIENTE TOWN

160
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:57,972
What's that?

161
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:00,558
[Dante] My project.

162
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,853
-Jessica Vergara?
-You know her?

163
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:06,314
Oh, um…

164
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:08,149
Her name sounds familiar.

165
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:11,110
Uh… [sighs]

166
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:14,071
What is it? Murder or rape?

167
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:17,241
Both. More than five years ago.

168
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:20,077
She went missing
until her body was found floating

169
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,579
in a river a week later.

170
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:25,041
Before that, she allegedly
had an affair with Raul Torillo.

171
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,376
There are plenty of other victims

172
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:30,171
that are connected to the Ardiente family.

173
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:31,589
You'll get in trouble for that.

174
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:39,430
[Camia] <i>Let go of me! Stop!</i>

175
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:40,848
[pot breaking]

176
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:43,559
[exhales]

177
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:47,355
Did your wife tell you
about what happened yesterday at school?

178
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:49,649
What?

179
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:57,615
Dante! You're home early.

180
00:10:59,992 --> 00:11:00,910
Are you tired?

181
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:03,621
Is it true you almost got raped yesterday?

182
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:04,580
[sighs]

183
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,917
Dante, it's over. Besides, nothing--

184
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,836
-Why didn't you tell me?
-I didn't want any trouble.

185
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,588
You're just going to keep quiet
after what he did?

186
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:15,341
-Nothing happened.
-He'll try again!

187
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:18,344
That was fun.

188
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:21,305
-I'll press charges!
-[Camia] Dante, let it go!

189
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,100
-Dad.
-Lily.

190
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:28,354
I'm with Diego.

191
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,482
Good afternoon.

192
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:40,491
[eerie music playing]

193
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,180
[gasps]

194
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:11,772
Don't worry. The wait is almost over.

195
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:13,983
Soon, I'll be able to avenge you.

196
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:16,152
[Dante] <i>Jessica Vergara?</i>

197
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,319
<i>She went missing,</i>

198
00:12:17,403 --> 00:12:19,780
<i>and her body was found floating</i>
<i>in a river a week later.</i>

199
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:24,660
<i>Before that, she allegedly</i>
<i>had an affair with Raul Torillo.</i>

200
00:12:28,706 --> 00:12:31,876
[Emilia] Congressman,
I heard that our rival party

201
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:34,295
has been raising funds for the election.

202
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:36,338
And there are two other candidates

203
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:39,383
who are running for governor,
Gopez and Marciano.

204
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,260
Don't mind them, Mayor.

205
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:43,762
They're just distractions in the election.

206
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:48,934
For sure, our people
still fully support the Ardientes.

207
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,519
[Emilia laughs]

208
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:51,812
[Julio] I agree.

209
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:57,902
I still believe that
our people are solid Ardiente supporters.

210
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,945
-Unwavering in their support. Solid.
-Solid.

211
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:03,949
So, when Emilia runs for governor,

212
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:09,163
Raul will be our next mayor.
Well, here's to victory!

213
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:10,998
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

214
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:12,500
[chuckles]

215
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:14,168
[clears throat]

216
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:15,878
-So, congressman.
-Hmm.

217
00:13:15,961 --> 00:13:19,465
Maybe you'd like to
introduce us to your companion.

218
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:20,591
Oh.

219
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,594
Everyone. This is Cinderella.

220
00:13:23,677 --> 00:13:25,679
Cindy for short.

221
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:28,516
-Cinderella! [laughs]
-Yes.

222
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,768
What an interesting name!

223
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:34,522
Is it because your appearance
changes at midnight?

224
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:36,315
[laughs]

225
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:38,943
Yes, Auntie. I become more beautiful.

226
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,070
[moans]

227
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:49,745
[Emilia] So, Congressman,
where did you meet your date?

228
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:54,083
[chuckles] Mayor,
Congressman Enriquez introduced her to me.

229
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:58,420
I see! No wonder
she looks so familiar to me.

230
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:02,800
[gentle piano music]

231
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:09,473
[tense music]

232
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:12,309
[sighs]

233
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:17,940
-Hi!
-[both laughing]

234
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:22,403
[Cindy] Slow down. I might slip.

235
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:23,988
-Take your shoes off. Come on.
-It's slippery.

236
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:26,323
[Cindy chuckles] Hold on!

237
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:29,368
Congressman, would you
please excuse me for a while?

238
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,328
-Oh, sure!
-Thank you.

239
00:14:33,247 --> 00:14:34,915
[Cindy giggling]

240
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,667
[Cindy] Hold on!

241
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:39,879
[tense music playing]

242
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:58,272
[Cindy moans]

243
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,276
[objects clatter]

244
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,671
What was that?

245
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:24,548
[Cindy] Something's burning. Let's go.

246
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,675
-Stop!
-Hey, wait!

247
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:28,886
-My hair is on fire!
-Wait. Hold on.

248
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:35,184
[Cindy] I said stop. I'm leaving!

249
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:37,061
-[Cindy] Where's it?
-[Raul] Fine, fine.

250
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:40,397
-Hey, where's my other shoe?
-I don't know!

251
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,739
[Emilia] Thank you so much
for coming. I hope you enjoyed dinner!

252
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:51,825
-Mayor, I have to go.
-Okay, Congressman.

253
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:53,535
[Emilia] Thank you. Thank you for coming.

254
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:55,329
Oh, by the way, Congressman,

255
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:57,831
your date seems to have
lost her other shoe.

256
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:12,721
Dante?

257
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:16,225
Please, let's not bring this to court.

258
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:19,603
They're powerful people.

259
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,274
ARDIENTE TOWN

260
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:28,737
Hello? I don't like it here.
I'm going back to Manila.

261
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:30,864
The Congressman's a cheapskate.

262
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:35,869
If you sue him,
we'll be the talk of the town.

263
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:37,997
It will affect Lily.

264
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:42,710
But if we both explain to her,
she'll understand.

265
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,628
Our daughter is smart.

266
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:46,880
She'll realize that
it's the right thing to do.

267
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,635
Yes, she's smart, just like you.

268
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:55,180
You're a great lawyer, but because of it,

269
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:57,016
a lot of people want to bring you down.

270
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,977
Hold on. I'll call you later, all right?

271
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,565
What's going on?
Why are they making me stop?

272
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:10,070
I'm scared I might see you dead
on the road one day.

273
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:13,615
Even when we're together, Dante…

274
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,160
[sighs] I'm still scared.

275
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:18,370
Because we could all get killed.

276
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:20,330
What is it?

277
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,957
[gunshot rings out]

278
00:17:23,959 --> 00:17:25,127
[Camia] Dante, please.

279
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:26,837
Please don't stir up trouble.

280
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,465
And now, it's my fault.

281
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:33,594
That's what's wrong with the mentality
of people nowadays!

282
00:17:33,677 --> 00:17:36,180
When violated, they just keep quiet

283
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:38,682
and allow themselves to become
victims over and over again!

284
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:42,644
Our passivity gives more power
to the wrong people!

285
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:46,106
We let them take advantage of us!

286
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:47,775
[Dante sighs]

287
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:54,907
Believe me. He'll keep trying
until he gets what he wants.

288
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:57,284
Camia, I'll fight for you.

289
00:17:58,243 --> 00:18:04,208
Dante. I will also fight
for a happy and peaceful life.

290
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,880
Are you arguing?

291
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:11,673
[sighs]

292
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:14,134
No, Lily.

293
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:27,481
[phone ringing]

294
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:29,441
-Hello?
-[gunman] <i>Good morning, ma'am.</i>

295
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,818
The job's done.

296
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,736
[reporter on TV] <i>Just this morning,</i>

297
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:35,280
<i>a woman's corpse was found</i>
<i>a few kilometers</i>

298
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,907
<i>outside the border of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

299
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,867
<i>The woman was identified</i>

300
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:42,162
<i>as Cinderella Madlang-awa</i>
<i>from Malate, Manila.</i>

301
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:43,205
Good job!

302
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:47,209
[tense music playing]

303
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:51,421
Poor Cinderella.

304
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,967
Oh. Breakfast?

305
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:57,553
It's the most important
meal of the day. Come.

306
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:08,230
[suspenseful music playing]

307
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:15,154
-Hi, Mom!
-Hi!

308
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:16,280
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

309
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:20,200
Mom, I found your shoe in the pool.

310
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:24,037
[scoffs] Son, you know
I don't wear cheap shoes.

311
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:28,834
Maid, can you throw this out?
Go wash your hands.

312
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:30,878
Good morning, Dad and Mom.

313
00:19:31,795 --> 00:19:34,131
Diego, where's your nanny?

314
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:35,716
She's inside.

315
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:38,010
Didn't she tell you that

316
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:41,388
from this day on, you're not
supposed to join us for meals?

317
00:19:41,471 --> 00:19:43,682
Seriously, Emilia? He's a kid!

318
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:45,726
Diego.

319
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,353
Your food will be brought to your room

320
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,647
so we can control what you eat.

321
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:53,817
Why so sad?

322
00:19:53,901 --> 00:19:55,360
You know I'm doing this for you, right?

323
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,906
Then, go back to your room now.

324
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:02,034
[sad music playing]

325
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:06,121
Come. Let's eat, son.

326
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:15,172
[Diego] What? Your family's leaving?

327
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:22,804
Yes.

328
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:26,850
I think so.

329
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:32,981
That's what I heard from Mom.

330
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:36,568
She said it'd be better if…

331
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:41,073
She said it'd be better if we left.

332
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:51,124
[cries]

333
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:54,962
Maybe it's not final yet.

334
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:57,756
I hope so.

335
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:01,551
I already like it here.

336
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:03,553
I don't want to leave.

337
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:08,934
I don't want to move houses again.

338
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,729
I thought we were finally
settling down here.

339
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:16,316
And if I leave,
who's going to be your friend?

340
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,694
[sniffles]

341
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:21,863
Who's going to exercise with you?

342
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:27,077
Who's going to help you
with your homework?

343
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,454
No one, that's for sure.

344
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:35,168
If you leave, no one
will make me happy anymore.

345
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:42,050
If you leave, I'll be alone.

346
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:46,346
I'll be lonely again.

347
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,603
I'll miss you.

348
00:21:56,148 --> 00:21:57,274
Me too.

349
00:22:00,193 --> 00:22:03,864
[Diego sobbing]

350
00:22:17,919 --> 00:22:19,212
[knocking]

351
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:24,092
[foreboding music playing]

352
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:27,095
-What are you doing here?
-Where's Diego?

353
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:29,056
He's not here.

354
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:35,228
Good.

355
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:37,689
Wait, why are you coming in?
[heavy breathing]

356
00:22:38,356 --> 00:22:39,900
I just want to give you these flowers.

357
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:47,657
I'm sorry. And thank you
for not filing a case against me.

358
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:53,205
I didn't do it because
our children are friends.

359
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:08,178
-How about us? Can we be friends?
-[panicked breathing]

360
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,430
Get away from me!

361
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:12,849
-Get out!
-[Raul] Hold on.

362
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:14,601
-You pervert!
-Wait!

363
00:23:14,684 --> 00:23:17,229
Let's not fool ourselves anymore.

364
00:23:17,312 --> 00:23:22,109
We both know that
we'll end up being friends.

365
00:23:24,027 --> 00:23:25,487
I said get out!

366
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:27,030
Camia, I just want to be friends with you.

367
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:28,615
-Can you please just leave?
-Why should I?

368
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:30,659
-Is it so wrong to be friends with you?
-Raul, stay away.

369
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:33,245
Stay away! Get your hands off me!

370
00:23:34,162 --> 00:23:35,747
[Camia shrieks]

371
00:23:35,831 --> 00:23:37,332
Go away!

372
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:39,084
-Look at you?
-[grunts]

373
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:41,711
-[Raul grunting]
-[Camia panting]

374
00:23:41,795 --> 00:23:42,629
[tense music]

375
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:45,549
[Lily] Mom!

376
00:23:46,883 --> 00:23:48,468
-Mom!
-Dad!

377
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:49,803
-You bastard!
-Dad!

378
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:51,805
-Dad!
-Dad, stop it!

379
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:53,765
-Stop it!
-Dad, please stop!

380
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:54,724
-Dad!
-Dad, no!

381
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,351
-[Camia] Stop!
-[Lily] Dad!

382
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:58,603
-Dad!
-Dad!

383
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:01,690
-[both men grunting]
-[Lily] Stop it! That's enough!

384
00:24:01,773 --> 00:24:05,068
-Dad!
-Dante, that's enough!

385
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:07,821
-Dad!
-Can you all leave us alone?

386
00:24:07,904 --> 00:24:10,323
-[Camia] Leave us alone!
-Please stop! Stop it!

387
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:12,784
-[Dante and Raul panting]
-[Lily] Stop it!

388
00:24:12,868 --> 00:24:16,371
I'll file a case against you. You'll see!

389
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:18,582
Come on. Let's go!

390
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:20,417
Diego!

391
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:24,629
[tense music playing]

392
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:31,928
Doc, I heard about what happened.

393
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:35,599
Nothing to worry about. I'll be on my way.

394
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,100
Okay. Thank you, Doc.

395
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:38,894
Thanks.

396
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:44,858
Can I see it?
The doctor said the cut isn't deep.

397
00:24:44,941 --> 00:24:47,068
-It's nothing.
-Show me.

398
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:50,947
-I said it's nothing.
-Is that so?

399
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:52,157
[Raul screams]

400
00:24:53,742 --> 00:24:57,746
[sighs] Diego, please go to your room now.

401
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:07,714
Honestly, I really wish
you'd use your head sometimes.

402
00:25:08,757 --> 00:25:10,926
You do know Dante Cruz is a lawyer, right?

403
00:25:11,009 --> 00:25:13,261
-So what?
-"So what"?

404
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:17,432
He can mean trouble for us.
He can talk about what happened

405
00:25:17,515 --> 00:25:20,769
and my political rivals can use that.

406
00:25:20,852 --> 00:25:22,646
It'll be a huge problem for my candidacy.

407
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:24,522
Are you an idiot?

408
00:25:25,273 --> 00:25:28,443
If I'm an idiot, then you talk too much.

409
00:25:28,526 --> 00:25:32,197
He won't be a problem. Have him killed!

410
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,407
-[scoffs]
-[pensive music]

411
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:42,249
[Dante] I told you he'd come back for you.

412
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,293
Are you okay?

413
00:25:46,628 --> 00:25:48,129
I'm okay, hon.

414
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:56,012
Dad, I can't believe
Diego's father is a bad person.

415
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:57,639
It's a good thing we saw him,

416
00:25:57,722 --> 00:26:00,350
or he could've done
something worse to Mom.

417
00:26:00,433 --> 00:26:01,935
Lily, you remember

418
00:26:02,018 --> 00:26:04,521
what I told you about
not trusting too easily, right?

419
00:26:06,481 --> 00:26:08,400
You have to be careful.

420
00:26:08,483 --> 00:26:10,735
You're a girl, and you're growing up fast.

421
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:16,157
If anyone touches you,
and you're not comfortable with it,

422
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:19,577
that's instinct telling you to get away.

423
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:22,580
I want you to learn
how to protect yourself

424
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:26,251
because your Mom and I
won't always be by your side.

425
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:31,047
Hon. I think Lily's too young for that.

426
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:32,841
Hon.

427
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:37,262
I want Lily to be prepared
for anything that might happen.

428
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:38,722
Promise me, Lily,

429
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:44,311
that you won't let yourself be abused

430
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,896
or harassed by anyone.

431
00:26:49,816 --> 00:26:51,109
I promise, Dad.

432
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:01,745
You called for me, Papa?

433
00:27:01,828 --> 00:27:03,246
It's the talk of the town.

434
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:08,251
Your devoted husband
couldn't keep his pants on again.

435
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:11,254
That man brings you nothing but shame.

436
00:27:12,380 --> 00:27:14,090
Fix this, Emilia.

437
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:17,135
Our political enemies
might catch wind of this.

438
00:27:17,218 --> 00:27:18,053
Yes, Papa.

439
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:22,265
That Dante Cruz,

440
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:26,186
he has already aggravated
a friend of mine from Manila.

441
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,272
He's not easy to silence.

442
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:32,817
-I'll take care of him, Papa.
-You do that.

443
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:38,031
For once, show me you've picked up
a thing or two from me.

444
00:27:38,114 --> 00:27:41,534
[tense music playing]

445
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,166
DON JULIO ARDIENTE
PILLAR OF ARDIENTE TOWN

446
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:52,879
Attorney Cruz, the Mayor's
inviting you to her office.

447
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:55,215
Hold on.

448
00:27:58,385 --> 00:28:01,304
[phone ringing]

449
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:03,390
Hello, Dante?

450
00:28:03,473 --> 00:28:06,518
Hon, I was on my way home,
but the mayor wants to see me.

451
00:28:06,601 --> 00:28:08,728
-What?
-[Dante] <i>I won't take long, hon.</i>

452
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:11,481
Don't worry about me. Goodbye.

453
00:28:12,273 --> 00:28:13,817
Hello? Dante?

454
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:15,693
[man] Let's go, sir.

455
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:17,570
Hello?

456
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:23,535
Mayor, Attorney Cruz is here.

457
00:28:24,911 --> 00:28:28,206
Attorney Dela Cruz! [chuckles]

458
00:28:28,289 --> 00:28:31,960
-It's Cruz, not Dela Cruz.
-I'm so sorry.

459
00:28:32,043 --> 00:28:35,505
I'm so bad with names.
I'm sure you understand.

460
00:28:35,588 --> 00:28:38,341
I have so many
responsibilities as the mayor.

461
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:39,300
Have a seat.

462
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:49,436
-What is this about, Mayor?
-Attorney.

463
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:52,439
We both know why I called you here.

464
00:28:52,522 --> 00:28:55,150
I'm sure you've heard
about the misunderstanding

465
00:28:55,233 --> 00:28:57,152
between your wife and my husband.

466
00:28:57,235 --> 00:29:00,363
What happened between
our spouses was no misunderstanding.

467
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:03,032
[scoffs] Whatever you call it, Attorney.

468
00:29:03,116 --> 00:29:07,871
But we both
want to avoid trouble, don't we?

469
00:29:07,954 --> 00:29:12,459
Maybe we can talk about this like adults.

470
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:15,170
We have nothing to talk about.
We're filing a lawsuit.

471
00:29:15,253 --> 00:29:21,551
[scoffs] Dante! Dante.
I can call you Dante, right?

472
00:29:21,634 --> 00:29:24,763
Besides, this is a personal conversation.

473
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:29,726
Honestly, I'm not doing this
for me or my family.

474
00:29:29,809 --> 00:29:31,686
I'm doing this for you.

475
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:36,775
I don't want you to waste
your time, resources, or effort.

476
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:39,235
I'm sorry to say this, Attorney.

477
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,654
But you won't win.

478
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:44,657
Truth and justice are on my side.

479
00:29:45,366 --> 00:29:48,578
Your position doesn't scare me,
even if you think you own this town.

480
00:29:48,661 --> 00:29:53,708
[chuckles] How charming.
He thinks he's fighting back.

481
00:29:54,375 --> 00:29:58,546
Calm down, Attorney.
You're too hot-headed.

482
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:01,966
All I'm saying is, don't waste your time.

483
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:05,136
Think about your family,
your beautiful wife,

484
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,222
and your young daughter.

485
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,848
They're precious.

486
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:11,434
Are you threatening me?

487
00:30:12,644 --> 00:30:16,856
I'm not afraid of you! Nor your family.

488
00:30:18,107 --> 00:30:19,400
Attorney.

489
00:30:19,484 --> 00:30:21,528
I've never been fond of making threats.

490
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,614
Go ahead if you want to fight
for what's right.

491
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:29,327
All I'm saying is,
I won't back down, either.

492
00:30:29,410 --> 00:30:31,621
[ominous music playing]

493
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:43,550
[tense music]

494
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:50,223
Arthur. What are you doing here?

495
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:55,144
The Mayor asked me to come.
I don't know why.

496
00:30:55,228 --> 00:30:56,521
But I'm a little worried.

497
00:30:57,063 --> 00:30:59,482
What about you? Why did she call you in?

498
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:05,280
[Dante sighs]

499
00:31:07,073 --> 00:31:08,199
Are you okay?

500
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:11,536
Here.

501
00:31:12,453 --> 00:31:13,413
Have some coffee.

502
00:31:13,496 --> 00:31:16,124
[ominous music playing]

503
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:33,474
[Arthur] Why are you here?

504
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:49,782
[breathing heavily]

505
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:51,409
[exhales heavily]

506
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:54,537
[phone ringing]

507
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:59,542
-Hello, hon?
-I'm on my way home, hon.

508
00:31:59,626 --> 00:32:01,002
Why is your voice shaking?

509
00:32:01,085 --> 00:32:02,462
[breathing heavily]

510
00:32:02,545 --> 00:32:05,048
-Hello, hon?
-[breathing heavily]

511
00:32:05,131 --> 00:32:06,841
-[breathing heavily]
-Dante?

512
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:08,635
[grunts]

513
00:32:08,718 --> 00:32:10,511
-Hello?
-[Dante grunting]

514
00:32:11,429 --> 00:32:12,513
Dante?

515
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:16,684
[tires screech]

516
00:32:16,768 --> 00:32:17,852
[vehicle crashes]

517
00:32:25,234 --> 00:32:27,278
IN LOVING MEMORY OF
CAMIA, LILY

518
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:28,529
Dad.

519
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:29,530
[Lily] <i>After the accident,</i>

520
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:32,659
<i>they conducted</i>
<i>an investigation and an autopsy.</i>

521
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:33,868
Dante.

522
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:35,370
<i>The results showed Dad</i>
<i>got into an accident…</i>

523
00:32:35,453 --> 00:32:36,287
Dante.

524
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,456
<i>…because he suffered a heart attack.</i>

525
00:32:38,539 --> 00:32:39,707
Dad.

526
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:49,550
[indistinct chatter]

527
00:32:51,094 --> 00:32:54,806
[indistinct chatter]

528
00:32:55,556 --> 00:32:57,100
-Hi, Mayor.
-Hello, Mayor.

529
00:32:57,183 --> 00:32:58,559
-Hi, friend.
-Good evening.

530
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,853
-Hello, Mayor
-Good evening. Hi. Sit down.

531
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:02,438
[man] Good evening, Mayor.

532
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:06,401
I'm sorry, Lily. My condolences.

533
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:11,406
-[sentimental music playing]
-Thank you.

534
00:33:18,329 --> 00:33:21,749
My condolences, Mrs. Cruz.
I'm sorry for your loss.

535
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:24,377
It must've been so painful for you, huh?

536
00:33:28,423 --> 00:33:29,799
How dare you?

537
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:32,343
You killed my husband!

538
00:33:32,927 --> 00:33:36,389
You murderers! You killed my husband!

539
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:38,057
What are you talking about?

540
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:41,728
-[Camia] You monsters!
-[Emilia shrieks, gasps]

541
00:33:41,811 --> 00:33:42,895
Leave! Get out of here!

542
00:33:42,979 --> 00:33:44,397
Mom, calm down.

543
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:45,565
[gasps]

544
00:33:46,983 --> 00:33:48,276
[Camia shouts] Get out!

545
00:33:48,359 --> 00:33:50,611
-Mom, please don't.
-[Raul] Let's go.

546
00:33:52,447 --> 00:33:54,657
It's okay. It's okay.

547
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:57,326
[people murmuring]

548
00:33:58,161 --> 00:33:59,829
-[man 1] Are you okay, Mayor?
-It's okay. It's okay.

549
00:33:59,912 --> 00:34:01,122
[Raul] It's okay, it's okay. Let's go.

550
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:02,457
[woman 1] Are you okay, Mayor?

551
00:34:04,751 --> 00:34:06,002
[woman 2] Mayor, are you okay?

552
00:34:06,085 --> 00:34:08,171
-I'm okay.
-[woman 3] Mayor…

553
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:17,555
[sentimental music playing]

554
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:19,182
[Lily sobbing]

555
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:21,893
Diego. Hurry up, okay?

556
00:34:21,976 --> 00:34:24,896
Your parents can't find out
we came back here.

557
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:26,939
I just asked the driver a favor.

558
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:32,487
[Lily sobbing]

559
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:37,617
Lily.

560
00:34:39,702 --> 00:34:40,620
Lily.

561
00:34:42,997 --> 00:34:47,752
[sentimental music playing]

562
00:34:52,799 --> 00:34:53,800
[stammering]

563
00:34:54,842 --> 00:34:56,344
He's gone…

564
00:34:59,889 --> 00:35:02,016
My father is gone now.

565
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,272
Why did Mom say…

566
00:35:09,649 --> 00:35:12,068
they killed Dad?

567
00:35:13,736 --> 00:35:16,239
[crying] I'm so sorry, Lily.

568
00:35:17,156 --> 00:35:19,951
I don't understand.

569
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:25,623
Sorry, Lily.
I don't know. I'm really sorry.

570
00:35:25,706 --> 00:35:28,334
[phone ringing]

571
00:35:30,253 --> 00:35:32,046
[Diego crying] I don't know!

572
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:39,053
[Lily wailing] He's dead!
It doesn't make sense!

573
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:40,680
I'm sorry, Lily!

574
00:35:40,763 --> 00:35:44,600
Diego. Your dad's calling, Diego.

575
00:35:45,518 --> 00:35:46,936
Lily!

576
00:35:49,188 --> 00:35:51,524
-[Loring] We have to go now.
-Lily!

577
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:57,989
My father!

578
00:35:58,072 --> 00:36:00,825
-[Loring] Let's go, Diego.
-Lily! I'm sorry!

579
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,661
[Diego crying] I'm sorry!

580
00:36:03,744 --> 00:36:07,540
-Diego! Sorry, Lily.
-Lily! I'm sorry!

581
00:36:10,209 --> 00:36:13,796
-I'm sorry!
-Let's go.

582
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:20,761
Bring back my father!

583
00:36:29,478 --> 00:36:32,148
[Lily crying]

584
00:36:32,231 --> 00:36:35,776
-[Lily crying]
-[Camia sobbing]

585
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:46,829
Dad.

586
00:36:51,125 --> 00:36:52,001
Mom.

587
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:58,716
[melancholic music playing]

588
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:08,100
[Camia crying]

589
00:37:11,312 --> 00:37:13,773
[Camia sobbing]

590
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:33,876
Mom.

591
00:37:35,836 --> 00:37:39,632
Mom, you haven't gone to work in weeks.

592
00:37:41,133 --> 00:37:43,594
I haven't been going to school.

593
00:37:46,555 --> 00:37:48,641
What's going to happen to us now?

594
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:51,477
I don't know.

595
00:37:52,395 --> 00:37:55,314
I don't know.

596
00:37:56,649 --> 00:37:58,734
What are you saying?

597
00:37:58,818 --> 00:38:01,529
-I don't know anymore!
-Mom.

598
00:38:01,612 --> 00:38:03,864
I don't know! I don't know!

599
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:05,700
I don't know!

600
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:11,497
[Camia wailing]

601
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:15,251
Please don't cry. Mom.

602
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:21,757
Please don't cry.

603
00:38:21,841 --> 00:38:23,217
[Camia wailing]

604
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:27,221
I'm sorry, Lily. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

605
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:34,103
Here's what we'll do.

606
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:37,565
Listen to me, Lily. Pack your things.

607
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:40,192
We're leaving as soon as possible.

608
00:38:40,276 --> 00:38:42,611
-Go on.
-Where will we go?

609
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:45,448
I don't know. Just pack up.

610
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:48,451
Hurry up! Go pack your things! Do it now!

611
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:49,910
Lily, hurry up!

612
00:38:50,870 --> 00:38:52,204
Hurry up!

613
00:38:53,122 --> 00:38:54,081
[shouts] Hurry!

614
00:38:54,999 --> 00:38:57,335
[Camia sobbing]

615
00:39:00,796 --> 00:39:02,214
Mom.

616
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:17,188
Lily, we'll go away.

617
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:20,483
That's what we should do now.

618
00:39:20,566 --> 00:39:24,236
Go out and look for anything we can bring.

619
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,738
Go on.

620
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:33,913
[Camia sobbing]

621
00:39:49,345 --> 00:39:54,141
[melancholic music playing]

622
00:39:57,144 --> 00:39:58,229
[Lily crying]

623
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:11,283
Dad.

624
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,705
Dad, it's Mom.

625
00:40:22,711 --> 00:40:27,007
[Lily] <i>She needs you, Dad. We need you.</i>

626
00:40:27,091 --> 00:40:29,260
<i>Please help us, Dad.</i>

627
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:33,389
I miss you so much, Dad!

628
00:40:34,765 --> 00:40:36,434
Dad!

629
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:40,479
Can you hear me from there?

630
00:40:42,022 --> 00:40:43,232
[Camia sobbing]

631
00:40:48,779 --> 00:40:51,449
I miss you so much, Dad!

632
00:40:52,408 --> 00:40:53,993
Dad!

633
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:07,548
Dante.

634
00:41:10,634 --> 00:41:14,221
[melancholic music playing]

635
00:41:14,305 --> 00:41:17,766
DEAR LILY

636
00:41:32,031 --> 00:41:34,200
[sobbing]

637
00:41:35,701 --> 00:41:36,994
[rustling]

638
00:41:38,954 --> 00:41:40,372
Dante?

639
00:41:40,456 --> 00:41:44,168
[foreboding music playing]

640
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:45,252
Who's there?

641
00:41:46,754 --> 00:41:47,796
Anybody there?

642
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:51,258
[foreboding music playing]

643
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,344
Who are you?

644
00:41:53,886 --> 00:41:55,804
-Don't be scared.
-Why?

645
00:41:57,348 --> 00:41:58,724
[gasps]

646
00:42:00,392 --> 00:42:01,227
We're going to have fun.

647
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,355
Don't come any closer, I'm begging you.

648
00:42:04,438 --> 00:42:05,356
[sobbing]

649
00:42:05,439 --> 00:42:06,857
We'll play a game.

650
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:10,736
Please don't.

651
00:42:10,819 --> 00:42:12,071
Don't.

652
00:42:12,988 --> 00:42:14,782
Stay away from me! No!

653
00:42:18,702 --> 00:42:23,624
[bleak music playing]

654
00:42:33,759 --> 00:42:36,595
[foreboding music playing]

655
00:42:40,724 --> 00:42:41,809
[suspenseful sting]

656
00:42:42,851 --> 00:42:45,938
[foreboding music playing]

657
00:42:50,609 --> 00:42:51,860
Mom?

658
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:54,196
Mom?

659
00:42:55,447 --> 00:42:56,657
[shushes]

660
00:42:56,740 --> 00:42:59,743
Lily. Get out of here. Go.

661
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:01,245
-Run away!
-What happened to you?

662
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:03,414
[shushes] Get out of here!

663
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:05,874
Run, Lily! Run!

664
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:08,377
-Mom, what happened to you?
-Get out of here!

665
00:43:08,460 --> 00:43:09,670
-Hey!
-[gasps]

666
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:12,715
Lily. Run!

667
00:43:12,798 --> 00:43:14,592
-Run!
-What are you doing here?

668
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:16,927
[Camia] Hurry up!

669
00:43:17,011 --> 00:43:17,845
[panting]

670
00:43:20,180 --> 00:43:21,140
[gun cocking]

671
00:43:24,393 --> 00:43:26,312
-Don't hurt my daughter!
-Let go of me!

672
00:43:26,395 --> 00:43:27,730
[grunts]

673
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:30,399
No!

674
00:43:32,901 --> 00:43:35,779
[Lily panting]

675
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:39,491
[suspenseful music playing]

676
00:43:40,826 --> 00:43:42,494
Mom.

677
00:43:42,578 --> 00:43:44,121
[whimpers]

678
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:55,966
Help. Help me!

679
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:01,305
Please help me! We need to save my mom!

680
00:44:01,388 --> 00:44:04,475
-Take a seat first.
-Mom is at our house.

681
00:44:04,558 --> 00:44:09,772
-Get her some water.
-Help her! Let's go back.

682
00:44:09,855 --> 00:44:12,149
POLICE

683
00:44:12,775 --> 00:44:17,071
-This way. She's inside.
-Wait for us here.

684
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,530
-Please hurry!
-Let's go.

685
00:44:21,075 --> 00:44:22,576
[Lily] <i>Mom? What happened to you?</i>

686
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:24,370
-[shushes]
-[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>

687
00:44:25,162 --> 00:44:27,373
<i>Lily. Run!</i>

688
00:44:27,456 --> 00:44:29,083
[echoing] <i>Mom…</i>

689
00:44:31,210 --> 00:44:32,461
Your mother's not inside.

690
00:44:32,544 --> 00:44:35,172
-But that's where I last saw her!
-[police officer] Let's go.

691
00:44:35,839 --> 00:44:37,633
-[Camia] <i>Hurry up!</i>
-[Lily] <i>Mom!</i>

692
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:41,136
[Camia] <i>Please don't hurt my daughter!</i>

693
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:43,138
-[Tonio] <i>Let go of me!</i>
-[Camia] <i>No!</i>

694
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:47,434
[crying] Mom. She was really here! Mom!

695
00:44:49,311 --> 00:44:51,688
Mom.

696
00:44:54,233 --> 00:44:56,735
Where is Mom?

697
00:44:58,278 --> 00:45:00,197
She was just there.

698
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:02,950
[wailing] Mom!

699
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:07,079
Mom!

700
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:11,250
Mom!

701
00:45:14,128 --> 00:45:17,589
[Raul] <i>You killed them all off?</i>
<i>You didn't even spare the kid.</i>

702
00:45:17,673 --> 00:45:19,299
[tires screech]

703
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:23,720
<i>To the people</i>
<i>who might know where Lily is…</i>

704
00:45:23,804 --> 00:45:26,849
[Julio]<i> You idiot!</i>
<i>You caused a huge scandal!</i>

705
00:45:26,932 --> 00:45:32,521
<i>People are talking about a child</i>
<i>missing from Poblacion Ardiente!</i>

706
00:45:32,604 --> 00:45:35,816
<i>I want justice for my mom and dad!</i>

707
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:36,775
<i>Then we have a deal.</i>

708
00:45:36,859 --> 00:45:40,988
<i>From now on, you'll be called Ivy Aguas.</i>

709
00:45:41,071 --> 00:45:44,700
[Lily] <i>This was the only way</i>
<i>for me to be reborn</i>

710
00:45:44,783 --> 00:45:46,869
<i>into a new me.</i>

711
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:50,080
[theme music playing]
